# A lexer for a small language, written the way a compiler written in
# SemanticScript would start: source text in, a list of tokens out, each token
# located by line and column. `writeListing` turns the tokens back into text,
# one line per token, which is what the lexfile entry writes to its output.
#
# Tokens: identifiers (a letter or `_`, then letters, digits, and `_`),
# integers (decimal digits that fit `Int64`), quoted text (`"` to `"` on one
# line, any UTF-8 inside), punctuation (one printable ASCII byte that is not a
# letter, digit, or space), and newlines. Spaces, tabs, and carriage returns
# separate tokens. The list always ends with an `endOfInput` token.
#
# Positions come from `string.advancePosition` (D-71): it steps over one whole
# UTF-8 character, so a column counts characters, not bytes, and a newline
# moves to column 1 of the next line.

lexer is module
lexer purpose "Split source text into tokens located by line and column, and list them as text"
lexer path lexer
lexer imports standard.string
lexer imports standard.byte
lexer imports standard.buffer
lexer imports standard.math
lexer imports standard.compare
lexer imports standard.logic
lexer imports standard.list
lexer imports standard.test
lexer exports TokenKind
lexer exports Token
lexer exports Tokens
lexer exports LexError
lexer exports tokenize
lexer exports writeListing

TokenKind is enum
TokenKind purpose "What a token is, with the value an integer or a punctuation mark carries"
TokenKind typeParameter none
TokenKind variant identifier none
TokenKind variant integer Int64
TokenKind variant text none
TokenKind variant punctuation Byte
TokenKind variant newline none
TokenKind variant endOfInput none

Token is record
Token purpose "One token: its kind, where its first character is, and how many bytes of source it covers"
Token typeParameter none
Token field kind TokenKind
Token field start string.Position
Token field length Int64

Tokens is typeInstance
Tokens purpose "The tokens of one source text, in source order"
Tokens instantiates list.List Token

LexError is enum
LexError purpose "Why tokenizing stopped, and where"
LexError typeParameter none
LexError variant invalidByte string.Position
LexError variant unterminatedText string.Position
LexError variant integerTooLarge string.Position

ByteRule is operationType
ByteRule purpose "A test that decides whether a byte continues the token being scanned"
ByteRule typeParameter none
ByteRule input value Byte copied
ByteRule output Bool
ByteRule outputOwnedBy none
ByteRule raises none
ByteRule effect none
ByteRule async false

